dia/commons/thumb/e/ef/POWIDZ_-_panoramio.jpg/960px-POWIDZ_-_panoramio.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/POWIDZ_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-POWIDZ_-_panoramio.jpg","caption":"Jezioro Powidzkie","author":"szwejk","licence":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:POWIDZ_-_panoramio.jpg","w":3872,"h":2592,"ok_print":true}],"intro":{"body":"Gniezno is a city in Greater Poland in Poland. It is traditionally regarded as having been the first capital of Poland, and has been witness to many important events in early Polish history. Gniezno has become the seat of the second Polish diocese (after Poznań) and the first archbishopric. The coronations of several kings of Poland took place in the Gniezno cathedral. Gniezno is situated in the northeastern part of the Greater Poland, between three lakes: Jelonek, Swietokrzyskie and Winiary, in what is called the Gniezno Lake District. It is only 50 kilometres away from Poznań and relatively close to Kujawsko-Pomorskie.","grounding":[{"source":"wikivoyage","title":"Gniezno","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Gniezno","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"short":"Gniezno is a historic city in Poland, led by the Primatial Basilica Metropolitan Cathedral of Gniezno. The Saint John the Baptist church in Gniezno rounds out about nine hours. Transport is good, and Jezioro Powidzkie suits a stay from May to September.","short_src":"rewrite","facts":{"population":70269,"visit_h":9.4}},"highlights":[{"id":"hl-primatial-basilica-metropolitan-cathedral-of-gniezno","name":"Primatial Basilica Metropolitan Cathedral of Gniezno","kind":"Cathedral","lat":52.53678,"lon":17.59264,"dist_km":0.7,"rank_score":7.78,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Bazylika_gnie%C5%BAnie%C5%84ska.jpg/960px-Bazylika_gnie%C5%BAnie%C5%84ska.jpg","author":"KH-10101","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licence_u